-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), lines 670 to 1126 (the end of s 23.3, the rest of Part I from s 24 to s 55, and
-- Part II) -- THE SEAT LAYER, piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has lost work, or cannot work because of sickness, pregnancy, caring for a child or a family member, or
-- who is self-employed or a fisher, asking whether they qualify for Employment Insurance benefits, how many hours or weeks they
-- need, how much they would receive and for how long, and what they must do or tell the Commission. For this range: when they
-- are disqualified or disentitled, what they may be penalised or made to repay, and what they must do to claim.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the
-- person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The layer-1 rules are called by name and nothing is
-- restated here; where a rule takes an input the person cannot state (a Period of days, a MAYBE), the question builds it in a
-- WHERE from the plain inputs.
--
-- WHAT A BOOLEAN ANSWER MEANS FOR A DEEMING RULE. Layer 1 answers a deeming or "no appeal" rule with JUST TRUE (it applies) or NOTHING
-- (it does not apply and the section says nothing). A question that asks "Does section N treat me as ...?" answers TRUE for JUST TRUE
-- and FALSE for NOTHING; FALSE then means "not by this provision", never "the opposite is true". The helper below does the conversion.
--
-- JUDGMENTS. What the Commission "considers", "is satisfied of" or "is of the opinion" is asked as a fact about what the Commission
-- has done or found ("Has the Commission found ...?"). Whether the person "had good cause", "had no reasonable alternative", or
-- whether an employment is "suitable" is asked as the person would answer it, and the answer the decider reaches may differ.
--
-- OFFICIALS HAVE NO SEAT. Where a provision is addressed to the Commission, the question is what the person is owed or exposed to.
-- The employer's provisions (ss 39 and 46(2)) and the directors' (s 46.1) are not asked here: they are layer 1 only. A later
-- seat layer for an employer, `ei2-seat-employer.l4`, would ask them.
--
-- The Act's own figures are the modules' own constants (7, 12 and 6 weeks, 700 hours, three weeks, 3 and 9 times, $12,000, 36 and
-- 72 months, 15 weeks, 60 months and 3 of 10 years). Amounts that the Act leaves to the Regulations or to the Commission (a rate of
-- weekly benefits, the hours required by section 7 or 7.1, the last day to claim) are asked as facts the person can find out, and
-- NOTES.md "Cross-references out of my ranges" says which piece decides each.

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` IS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST b   THEN b

-- The kind of employment support measure, if the person is under one: built from a yes/no and a choice.
GIVEN underOne IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
GIVETH A MAYBE `ei2 Kind of employment support measure`
DECIDE `ei2 seat: the measure the person is under, if any` IS
    IF underOne THEN JUST kind ELSE NOTHING

-- A period of days from its first and last day.
GIVEN firstDay IS A DATE
      lastDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `ei2 seat: the period from the first day to the last day` IS
    `Period of days` OF firstDay, lastDay

§ `Employment Insurance Act -- the claimant's questions on ss 23.3(6) to 65.2`

§§ `Dividing the weeks of benefits for caring for a critically ill adult (s 23.3(6) to (9))`
-- This group only arises if the person is, or is about to be, claiming benefits for caring for or supporting a critically ill adult
-- (s 23.3), so the form can ask "Are you claiming benefits to care for a critically ill adult?" before showing it.

-- s 23.3(6). "Remaining weeks": the weeks still payable for this adult under s 23.3, s 152.062 or both. Up to 15 may be divided.
@export How many of the remaining weeks of benefits can another claimant and I divide between us (s 23.3(6))?
GIVEN `I am claiming benefits for caring for or supporting a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making a claim for benefits under section 23.3, for caring for or supporting a critically ill adult?
      `another person is claiming for the same adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another person claiming benefits for the same adult, under section 23.3, or under section 152.062 if they are self-employed?
      `the weeks of benefits remaining` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of benefits remain payable for this adult, under section 23.3, section 152.062 or both together?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many of the remaining weeks can we divide between us` IS
    `s 23.3(6) the number of remaining weeks that may be divided`
        `I am claiming benefits for caring for or supporting a critically ill adult`
        `another person is claiming for the same adult`
        `the weeks of benefits remaining`

@export Do the prescribed rules, and not our agreement, decide how the remaining weeks are divided between another claimant and me (s 23.3(6))?
GIVEN `we have agreed how to divide the weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the other claimant and you agreed how to divide the remaining weeks between you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do the prescribed rules decide how the weeks are divided` IF
    `s 23.3(6) the way the remaining weeks are divided` `we have agreed how to divide the weeks` EQUALS `ei2 divided in accordance with the prescribed rules`

@export Would dividing this many weeks go over the 15-week ceiling in section 23.3(7)?
GIVEN `I am claiming under section 23.3 for an adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming benefits under section 23.3 for an adult?
      `another person is claiming under section 152.062 for the same adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is another person, who is self-employed, claiming benefits under section 152.062 for the same adult?
      `the total weeks we would divide` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks in total, under section 23.3 and section 152.062 together, would you divide between you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would dividing this many weeks go over the ceiling` IF
    `s 23.3(7) the total number of weeks divided is within the ceiling`
        `I am claiming under section 23.3 for an adult`
        `another person is claiming under section 152.062 for the same adult`
        `the total weeks we would divide`
    EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 23.3(8). The reason is fixed by the section (sections 23.1 and 152.06 are compassionate care benefits); any other reason gives
-- the same answer, so a placeholder reason (regular benefits) stands for "not compassionate care".
@export Are compassionate care benefits unpayable to me for this week because of the critically ill adult (s 23.3(8))?
GIVEN `I am claiming compassionate care benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming compassionate care benefits (for caring for or supporting a gravely ill family member)?
      `my claim is in respect of the adult for whom the period was set` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for the same adult for whom the s 23.3(3) or 152.062(3) period was established?
      `the Sunday of the week I claim for` IS A DATE @desc Which week are you claiming for? Give the Sunday that begins it (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-01).
      `the first day of the adult's period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the period established for the critically ill adult under section 23.3(3) or 152.062(3)? It is the Sunday of the first week (ISO 8601).
      `the last day of the adult's period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of that period? It is the Saturday of the last week (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are compassionate care benefits unpayable to me this week` IF
    `s 23.3(8) benefits under section 23.1 or 152.06 are not payable`
        (IF `I am claiming compassionate care benefits` THEN `care or support of a family member` ELSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)`)
        `my claim is in respect of the adult for whom the period was set`
        `the Sunday of the week I claim for`
        (`ei2 seat: the period from the first day to the last day` `the first day of the adult's period` `the last day of the adult's period`)

@export Will my benefits under section 23.3 be reduced or eliminated because I am entitled to payments under a provincial law (s 23.3(9))?
GIVEN `benefits are payable to me for caring for a critically ill adult` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you under section 23.3, for caring for or supporting a critically ill adult?
      `payments are payable to me under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are allowances, money or other benefits payable to you under a provincial law?
      `they are for the same or substantially the same reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those payments for the same or substantially the same reasons?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my benefits be reduced or eliminated because of a provincial law` IF
    `s 23.3(9) the benefits payable under section 23.3 are to be reduced or eliminated as prescribed`
        `benefits are payable to me for caring for a critically ill adult`
        `payments are payable to me under a provincial law`
        `they are for the same or substantially the same reasons`

§§ `Work-sharing, courses, programs and employment support measures (ss 24 to 26)`
-- The first two questions only arise if the person works under a work-sharing agreement; the next three if the person is attending a
-- course, program or activity the Commission referred them to.

@export Does section 24(3) treat me as unemployed and capable of and available for work in a week when I work in work-sharing employment?
GIVEN `I work in work-sharing employment this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you work in work-sharing employment this week (employment under a work-sharing agreement the Commission has approved)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 24(3) treat me as unemployed and available this week` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 24(3) the claimant is unemployed and capable of and available for work during the week` `I work in work-sharing employment this week`)

@export Is the Commission's direction approving or disapproving a work-sharing agreement closed to review under section 112 (s 24(2))?
GIVEN `the decision is a direction on a work-sharing agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a special or general direction of the Commission approving or disapproving a work-sharing agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the direction on a work-sharing agreement closed to review` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 24(2) the direction on a work sharing agreement is not subject to review under section 112` `the decision is a direction on a work-sharing agreement`)

@export Does section 25(1) treat me as unemployed and available for work while I attend a course or program the Commission referred me to?
GIVEN `I am attending a course or program of instruction or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you attending a course or program of instruction or training?
      `I am paying for it myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paying for the course or program yourself?
      `it is given under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given under an employment support measure?
      `the kind of that employment support measure` IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure` @desc If it is under an employment support measure, what kind is it? One of: "ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training", "ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support", "ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services", "ei2 s 59(d) measure supporting research, innovation or partnerships", "ei2 an employment support measure not described in paragraphs 59(a) to (d)". If it is under none, give any one.
      `it is under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it given under a measure that is the subject of an agreement between the Commission and a government or organization under section 63?
      `the Commission or an authority it designates referred me to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission, or an authority it designates, refer you to the course or program?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 25(1)(a) treat me as unemployed and available during my course` IF
    `s 25(1)(a) attending a referred course or program of instruction or training`
        `I am attending a course or program of instruction or training`
        `I am paying for it myself`
        (`ei2 seat: the measure the person is under, if any` `it is given under an employment support measure` `the kind of that employment support measure`)
        `it is under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63`
        `the Commission or an authority it designates referred me to it`

@export Does section 25(1) treat me as unemployed and available for work while I take part in an employment activity the Commission referred me to?
GIVEN `I am taking part in an employment activity other than a course or program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you participating in an employment activity other than a course or program of instruction or training?
      `assistance for it comes from an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has assistance been provided for you under an employment support measure?
      `the kind of the measure that gave the assistance` IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure` @desc If assistance comes from an employment support measure, what kind is it? One of: "ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training", "ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support", "ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services", "ei2 s 59(d) measure supporting research, innovation or partnerships", "ei2 an employment support measure not described in paragraphs 59(a) to (d)". If none, give any one.
      `that measure is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that measure one the Regulations prescribe for this purpose (regulation 50)?
      `the assistance is under a prescribed measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the assistance given under a prescribed measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63?
      `the Commission or an authority it designates referred me to the activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission, or an authority it designates, refer you to the activity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 25(1)(b) treat me as unemployed and available during my activity` IF
    `s 25(1)(b) participating in a referred employment activity`
        `I am taking part in an employment activity other than a course or program`
        (`ei2 seat: the measure the person is under, if any` `assistance for it comes from an employment support measure` `the kind of the measure that gave the assistance`)
        `that measure is prescribed`
        `the assistance is under a prescribed measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63`
        `the Commission or an authority it designates referred me to the activity`

@export Is the Commission's decision about my referral to a course, program or activity closed to review under section 112 (s 25(2))?
GIVEN `the decision is about my referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a decision of the Commission about referring you to a course, program or other employment activity mentioned in section 25(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the decision about my referral closed to review` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 25(2) the decision about the referral is not subject to review under section 112` `the decision is about my referral`)

@export Does section 26 say the benefits I am paid while employed under an employment support measure are not earnings?
GIVEN `I am paid benefits while employed under a measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you paid benefits while you are employed under an employment support measure, or under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63?
      `I am employed under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under an employment support measure (as opposed to a measure that is the subject of a section 63 agreement)?
      `the kind of the measure I am employed under` IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure` @desc If you are employed under an employment support measure, what kind is it? One of: "ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training", "ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support", "ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services", "ei2 s 59(d) measure supporting research, innovation or partnerships", "ei2 an employment support measure not described in paragraphs 59(a) to (d)". If none, give any one.
      `I am employed under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 26 say my benefits are not earnings` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies`
        (`s 26 the benefits paid are not earnings from employment`
            `I am paid benefits while employed under a measure`
            (`ei2 seat: the measure the person is under, if any` `I am employed under an employment support measure` `the kind of the measure I am employed under`)
            `I am employed under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63`)

§§ `Being disqualified for not looking for work, or for a referral that ended (ss 27 and 28)`

@export Am I disqualified from receiving benefits because, without good cause, I did not apply for or accept suitable work, take an opportunity, follow a direction or attend an interview (s 27(1))?
GIVEN `I had no good cause for what I did or did not do since my interruption of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since your interruption of earnings, did you act (or fail to act) without good cause in any of the ways below?
      `I have not applied for suitable work that is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a suitable employment that is vacant that you have not applied for, after you became aware that it was vacant or it became vacant?
      `I failed to accept suitable work offered to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed to accept a suitable employment that was offered to you?
      `I have not taken advantage of an opportunity for suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not taken advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment?
      `the Commission gave me a written direction to help me find suitable work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission give you a written direction with a view to helping you find suitable employment?
      `I have not carried out that direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not carried out that direction?
      `that direction was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the direction reasonable, having regard both to your circumstances and to the usual means of obtaining that employment?
      `the Commission directed me to attend an interview` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission direct you to attend an interview?
      `the interview was to give me information and instruction to help me find work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interview to give you information and instruction to help you find employment?
      `the interview was to see whether job training or other employment assistance could help me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the interview to identify whether you might be assisted by job training or other employment assistance?
      `I did not attend the interview` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not attend the interview?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified because of what I did or did not do since my interruption of earnings` IF
    `s 27(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I`
        `I had no good cause for what I did or did not do since my interruption of earnings`
        (`s 27(1)(a) not applying for or accepting a suitable employment` `I have not applied for suitable work that is vacant` `I failed to accept suitable work offered to me`)
        (`s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment` `I have not taken advantage of an opportunity for suitable work`)
        (`s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission` `the Commission gave me a written direction to help me find suitable work` `I have not carried out that direction` `that direction was reasonable`)
        (`s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission` `the Commission directed me to attend an interview` `the interview was to give me information and instruction to help me find work` `the interview was to see whether job training or other employment assistance could help me` `I did not attend the interview`)

@export Am I disqualified from receiving benefits because the Commission ended my referral to a course, program or activity (s 27(1.1))?
GIVEN `the Commission or an authority it designates referred me with my agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission, or an authority it designates, refer you, with your agreement, to a course or program of instruction or training or to another employment activity?
      `the activity is assisted under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was assistance provided for it under an employment support measure?
      `the kind of that employment support measure` IS A `ei2 Kind of employment support measure` @desc If so, what kind is the measure? One of: "ei2 s 59(a) measure providing courses or programs of instruction or training", "ei2 s 59(b) measure providing employment opportunities or employment support", "ei2 s 59(c) measure providing employment assistance services", "ei2 s 59(d) measure supporting research, innovation or partnerships", "ei2 an employment support measure not described in paragraphs 59(a) to (d)". If none, give any one.
      `the Commission ended the referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission end the referral?
      `I did not attend or take part without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, without good cause, not attend or take part in the course, program or activity?
      `the Commission thinks I am unlikely to complete it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Commission's opinion, is it unlikely that you will successfully complete it?
      `I withdrew without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you withdraw from it without good cause?
      `the organization providing it expelled me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the organization providing it expel you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified because my referral to a course, program or activity ended` IF
    `s 27(1.1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving benefits under Part I`
        (`s 27(1.1)(a) a referral with the claimant's agreement to an activity assisted under a measure other than one in paragraph 59(c)`
            `the Commission or an authority it designates referred me with my agreement`
            (`ei2 seat: the measure the person is under, if any` `the activity is assisted under an employment support measure` `the kind of that employment support measure`))
        (`s 27(1.1)(b) the Commission has terminated the referral for one of the stated reasons`
            `the Commission ended the referral`
            `I did not attend or take part without good cause`
            `the Commission thinks I am unlikely to complete it`
            `I withdrew without good cause`
            `the organization providing it expelled me`)

@export What is the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows for my ground (s 28(1))? There is an answer only for grounds (a) and (b); for the others the Act states no least number and the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN `my ground of disqualification` IS A `ei2 Ground of disqualification under section 27` @desc Which ground applies to you? One of: "ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment", "ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment", "ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission", "ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission", "ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated".
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` IS
    `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `my ground of disqualification`

@export Does section 28(1) set a least number of weeks of disqualification for my ground?
GIVEN `my ground of disqualification` IS A `ei2 Ground of disqualification under section 27` @desc Which ground applies to you? One of: "ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment", "ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment", "ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission", "ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission", "ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 28(1) set a least number of weeks for my ground` IF
    CONSIDER `s 28(1) the fewest weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `my ground of disqualification`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n   THEN TRUE

@export What is the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows for my ground (s 28(1))?
GIVEN `my ground of disqualification` IS A `ei2 Ground of disqualification under section 27` @desc Which ground applies to you? One of: "ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment", "ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment", "ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission", "ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission", "ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated".
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` IS
    `s 28(1) the most weeks of disqualification the Act allows` `my ground of disqualification`

@export Is the number of weeks of disqualification the Commission set within what the Act allows (s 28(1))?
GIVEN `my ground of disqualification` IS A `ei2 Ground of disqualification under section 27` @desc Which ground applies to you? One of: "ei2 s 27(1)(a) not applying for, or not accepting, a suitable employment", "ei2 s 27(1)(b) not taking advantage of an opportunity for suitable employment", "ei2 s 27(1)(c) not carrying out a written direction of the Commission", "ei2 s 27(1)(d) not attending an interview directed by the Commission", "ei2 s 27(1.1) referral to a course, program or activity terminated".
      `the number of weeks the Commission set` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of disqualification has the Commission determined?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the number of weeks the Commission set within what the Act allows` IF
    `s 28(1) the number of weeks determined is within the limits of the Act` `my ground of disqualification` `the number of weeks the Commission set`

@export Is this week one of the weeks of my section 27 disqualification that I must serve (s 28(2))?
GIVEN `my disqualification is for this many weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks is your disqualification?
      `this is the nth week following my waiting period for which I would otherwise be paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Counting only the weeks after your waiting period for which you would otherwise be paid benefits, and leaving out any week you are otherwise entitled to special benefits or benefits under section 25, what number is this week (1 for the first)?
      `I am otherwise entitled to benefits this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the disqualification, are you otherwise entitled to benefits this week?
      `the reason for those benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc For what reason would you otherwise get those benefits? One of: "a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)" (regular benefits), "pregnancy", "caring for a new-born or adopted child", "a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine", "care or support of a family member", "care or support of a critically ill child", "care or support of a critically ill adult". If you are not otherwise entitled to any benefits give any one.
      `I am otherwise entitled to benefits under section 25 this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you otherwise entitled to benefits this week because you are attending a course, program or activity referred to in section 25?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this week one I must serve as a week of disqualification` IF
    `s 28(2) the week is served as a week of disqualification`
        `my disqualification is for this many weeks`
        `this is the nth week following my waiting period for which I would otherwise be paid`
        (`s 28(5) the serving of the disqualification is deferred` `I am otherwise entitled to benefits this week` `the reason for those benefits` `I am otherwise entitled to benefits under section 25 this week`)

@export How many weeks of my disqualification carry forward into a later benefit period (s 28(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the weeks of my disqualification still unserved when my benefit period ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of your disqualification had not been served when your benefit period ended?
      `the day of the event that led to the disqualification` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the event that gave rise to your disqualification happen (ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-15)?
      `the first day of my later benefit period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of the later benefit period established for you (ISO 8601)?
      `my hours of insurable employment since that event` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment have you had since that event?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many weeks of my disqualification carry forward` IS
    `s 28(3) the weeks of disqualification carried forward into the later benefit period`
        `the weeks of my disqualification still unserved when my benefit period ended`
        `the day of the event that led to the disqualification`
        `the first day of my later benefit period`
        `my hours of insurable employment since that event`

@export Are benefits treated as paid to me for a week of my disqualification (s 28(6))?
GIVEN `this is a week of my disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the week one of the weeks for which you are disqualified under section 27?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are benefits treated as paid to me for this week of disqualification` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 28(6) benefits are deemed to be paid for the week` `this is a week of my disqualification`)

@export Can I still ask to cancel a minor-attachment benefit period and have a major-attachment one established to receive special benefits (s 28(7))?
GIVEN `my benefit period was established as a minor attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your benefit period established with fewer than 600 hours (as a minor attachment claimant)?
      `I ask to cancel it under section 10(6) and have one established as a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking that it be cancelled under subsection 10(6) and that a benefit period be established for you as a major attachment claimant?
      `I want to receive special benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you want to receive special benefits (sickness, maternity, parental, caregiving)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I still make the request despite the deeming of benefits as paid` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies`
        (`s 28(7) the deeming of benefits as paid is no bar to the request`
            `my benefit period was established as a minor attachment claimant`
            `I ask to cancel it under section 10(6) and have one established as a major attachment claimant`
            `I want to receive special benefits`)

§§ `Losing or leaving a job: misconduct, leaving without just cause, suspension and leave (ss 29 to 35)`
-- This group only arises if the person lost a job, was suspended, took leave or left a job, so the form can ask "Did you lose, leave
-- or take leave from a job?" before showing it.

@export Is this employment one that counts under sections 30 to 33 (s 29(a))?
GIVEN `it falls within my qualifying period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employment within your qualifying period?
      `it falls within my benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the employment within your benefit period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this employment one that counts under sections 30 to 33` IF
    `s 29(a) the employment is an employment for the purposes of sections 30 to 33` `it falls within my qualifying period` `it falls within my benefit period`

@export Does the Act count what happened as the loss of my employment (s 29(b))?
GIVEN `I lost the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose the employment (for example, you were dismissed or laid off)?
      `I was suspended from the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you suspended from the employment?
      `it was on account of union membership or lawful union activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the loss or suspension on account of your membership in, or lawful activity connected with, an association, organization or union of workers?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act count what happened as the loss of my employment` IF
    `s 29(b) loss of employment` `I lost the employment` `I was suspended from the employment` `it was on account of union membership or lawful union activity`

@export Does the Act count what I did as voluntarily leaving my employment (s 29(b.1))?
GIVEN `I left the employment of my own choice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave the employment of your own choice?
      `I refused employment offered as an alternative to an expected loss of my job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse employment offered as an alternative to an anticipated loss of your employment?
      `I refused to resume the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse to resume the employment?
      `I refused to continue after the business was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse to continue in the employment after the work, undertaking or business of the employer was transferred to another employer?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act count what I did as voluntarily leaving my employment` IF
    `s 29(b.1) voluntarily leaving an employment` `I left the employment of my own choice` `I refused employment offered as an alternative to an expected loss of my job` `I refused to resume the employment` `I refused to continue after the business was transferred`

@export On what day does my refusal count as my voluntarily leaving the employment (s 29(b.1))?
GIVEN `I refused employment offered as an alternative to an expected loss of my job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse employment offered as an alternative to an anticipated loss of your employment?
      `the day my job was lost` IS A DATE @desc On what day did (or will) the loss of your employment occur (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-05-29)?
      `I refused to resume the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse to resume the employment?
      `the day I was supposed to resume` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you supposed to resume the employment (ISO 8601)?
      `I refused to continue after the business was transferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you refuse to continue in the employment after the work, undertaking or business was transferred to another employer?
      `the day the business was transferred` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the work, undertaking or business transferred (ISO 8601)?
      `the day I actually left` IS A DATE @desc If none of those refusals applies, on what day did you actually leave (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my refusal count as my voluntarily leaving` IS
    -- Where none of the three refusals applies the section gives no rule for the day, and the day the person left is the answer.
    CONSIDER `s 29(b.1) the day on which a refusal counts as the voluntary leaving` `I refused employment offered as an alternative to an expected loss of my job` `the day my job was lost` `I refused to resume the employment` `the day I was supposed to resume` `I refused to continue after the business was transferred` `the day the business was transferred`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `the day I actually left`
    WHEN JUST d   THEN d

@export Did I have just cause for voluntarily leaving my employment or taking leave from it (s 29(c))?
GIVEN `I had no reasonable alternative to leaving or taking leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Having regard to all the circumstances, did you have no reasonable alternative to leaving or taking leave? The decider's view of this is what the Act turns on.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I have just cause for leaving or taking leave` IF
    `s 29(c) just cause for voluntarily leaving an employment or taking leave exists` `I had no reasonable alternative to leaving or taking leave`

@export Is one of the circumstances the Act lists as relevant to just cause present in my case (s 29(c))? A yes does not by itself prove just cause.
GIVEN `I suffered sexual or other harassment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer sexual or other harassment?
      `I had to accompany a spouse, partner or dependent child to another residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an obligation to accompany a spouse, common-law partner or dependent child to another residence?
      `I suffered discrimination on a prohibited ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer discrimination on a prohibited ground of discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act?
      `my working conditions were a danger to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were your working conditions a danger to health or safety?
      `I had to care for a child or a member of my immediate family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have an obligation to care for a child or a member of your immediate family?
      `I had reasonable assurance of another job in the immediate future` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable assurance of another employment in the immediate future?
      `my wages or salary terms were significantly changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the terms and conditions respecting your wages or salary significantly modified?
      `I faced excessive overtime or refusal to pay for overtime` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you face excessive overtime work, or a refusal to pay for overtime work?
      `my work duties changed significantly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your work duties change significantly?
      `I had antagonism with a supervisor that was not mainly my doing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there antagonism with a supervisor of which you were not primarily responsible?
      `my employer did things contrary to law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were there practices of your employer that are contrary to law?
      `I suffered discrimination because of union membership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you suffer discrimination with regard to employment because of your membership in an association, organization or union of workers?
      `my employer unduly pressed me to leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer put undue pressure on you to leave your employment?
      `another prescribed circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another reasonable circumstance prescribed by the Regulations apply (regulation 51.1: an obligation to accompany a partner of less than a year who has had or adopted, or is expecting, a child, or an obligation to care for a member of your immediate family)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is one of the circumstances the Act lists present` IF
    `s 29(c) one of the circumstances listed in the Act is present`
        `I suffered sexual or other harassment`
        `I had to accompany a spouse, partner or dependent child to another residence`
        `I suffered discrimination on a prohibited ground`
        `my working conditions were a danger to health or safety`
        `I had to care for a child or a member of my immediate family`
        `I had reasonable assurance of another job in the immediate future`
        `my wages or salary terms were significantly changed`
        `I faced excessive overtime or refusal to pay for overtime`
        `my work duties changed significantly`
        `I had antagonism with a supervisor that was not mainly my doing`
        `my employer did things contrary to law`
        `I suffered discrimination because of union membership`
        `my employer unduly pressed me to leave`
        `another prescribed circumstance applies`

@export Am I disqualified from receiving any benefits because I lost a job through my misconduct or left one without just cause (s 30(1))?
GIVEN `I lost a job because of my misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose any employment because of your misconduct?
      `I left a job without just cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily leave any employment without just cause?
      `my only reason for being disqualified is that I left or refused a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your only possible reason for being disqualified that you left, or refused to accept, an employment?
      `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to join, or not join, a union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By remaining in or accepting the employment, would you have lost the right to become, or refrain from becoming, a member of an association, organization or union of workers?
      `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to stay in and follow the rules of my union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By remaining in or accepting the employment, would you have lost the right to continue to be a member of such a union and to observe its lawful rules?
      `my hours of insurable employment since losing or leaving` IS A NUMBER @desc Since you lost or left the employment, how many hours of insurable employment have you had?
      `the hours I need to qualify` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you need to qualify for benefits (section 7 or 7.1; it depends on the regional rate of unemployment and any violation)?
      `I am disentitled under sections 31 to 33 for that job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disentitled under section 31, 32 or 33 in relation to that employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I disqualified because I lost a job through misconduct or left without just cause` IF
    `s 30(1) the claimant is disqualified from receiving any benefits`
        `I lost a job because of my misconduct`
        `I left a job without just cause`
        (`ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies`
            (`s 35 the claimant is not disqualified or disentitled under sections 30 to 33`
                `my only reason for being disqualified is that I left or refused a job`
                `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to join, or not join, a union`
                `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to stay in and follow the rules of my union`))
        `my hours of insurable employment since losing or leaving`
        `the hours I need to qualify`
        `I am disentitled under sections 31 to 33 for that job`

@export Is this week one of the weeks for which I am disqualified under section 30 (s 30(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `I am disqualified under section 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disqualified under section 30(1)?
      `the Sunday of the week` IS A DATE @desc Which week? Give the Sunday that begins it (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-03-08).
      `the first day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your benefit period (ISO 8601)?
      `the last day of my benefit period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your benefit period (ISO 8601)?
      `the first day of my waiting period` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day of your waiting period (ISO 8601)?
      `the last day of my waiting period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of your waiting period (ISO 8601)?
      `the event happened during a benefit period of mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the event that gave rise to the disqualification (the loss or leaving) happen during a benefit period of yours?
      `the day of the event` IS A DATE @desc On what day did that event happen (ISO 8601)?
      `I am otherwise entitled to benefits this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the disqualification, are you otherwise entitled to benefits for this week?
      `the reason for those benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc For what reason would you otherwise get those benefits? One of: "a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)" (regular benefits), "pregnancy", "caring for a new-born or adopted child", "a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine", "care or support of a family member", "care or support of a critically ill child", "care or support of a critically ill adult". If you are not otherwise entitled to any benefits give any one.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this week one for which I am disqualified under section 30` IF
    `s 30(2) to (4) the week is a week of disqualification`
        `I am disqualified under section 30(1)`
        (`s 30(2) the week is a week of the benefit period following the waiting period`
            `the Sunday of the week`
            (`ei2 seat: the period from the first day to the last day` `the first day of my benefit period` `the last day of my benefit period`)
            (`ei2 seat: the period from the first day to the last day` `the first day of my waiting period` `the last day of my waiting period`))
        (`s 30(3) the week is not a week before the week in which the event occurs` `the event happened during a benefit period of mine` `the day of the event` `the Sunday of the week`)
        (`s 30(4) the disqualification is suspended for the week` `I am otherwise entitled to benefits this week` `the reason for those benefits`)

@export How many hours of insurable employment can I use to qualify after losing or leaving a job as described in section 30(1) (s 30(5))?
GIVEN `my hours in the job I lost or left and any job before it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in the employment you lost or left, and in any other employment before it was lost or left?
      `my hours in a later job I also lost or left` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in any later employment that you also lost or left in the way described in section 30(1)?
      `my hours in jobs I did not lose or leave in that way` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment have you had in jobs you did not lose or leave in that way?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours can I use to qualify after losing or leaving a job` IS
    -- The two gates of s 30(5) (a loss or leaving as described, and an initial claim) are the premise of the question; with the three
    -- parts of the total given separately the hours cannot be inconsistent, so the NOTHING arm cannot be reached; if it were, the
    -- answer would be the hours in jobs not lost or left, which is what the rule gives.
    CONSIDER `s 30(5) the hours that may be used to qualify under section 7 or 7.1` TRUE TRUE (`my hours in the job I lost or left and any job before it` PLUS `my hours in a later job I also lost or left` PLUS `my hours in jobs I did not lose or leave in that way`) `my hours in the job I lost or left and any job before it` `my hours in a later job I also lost or left`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `my hours in jobs I did not lose or leave in that way`
    WHEN JUST h   THEN h

@export How many of my hours can be used to work out my maximum weeks and my rate of weekly benefits after I lost or left a job as described in section 30(1) (s 30(6))?
GIVEN `my hours in jobs I lost or left in that way` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in employment that you lost or left as described in section 30(1)?
      `my hours in other jobs` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment did you have in other employment?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours can be used for my maximum weeks and my rate` IS
    -- With the two parts of the total given separately, the hours cannot be inconsistent, so the NOTHING arm cannot be reached; if it were,
    -- the answer would be the hours in other jobs, which is what the rule gives.
    CONSIDER `s 30(6) the hours that may be used to determine the maximum weeks and the rate of weekly benefits` (`my hours in jobs I lost or left in that way` PLUS `my hours in other jobs`) `my hours in jobs I lost or left in that way`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `my hours in other jobs`
    WHEN JUST h   THEN h

@export Am I not entitled to receive benefits because I am suspended from my job for misconduct (s 31)?
GIVEN `I am suspended from my job because of my misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you suspended from your employment because of your misconduct?
      `my period of suspension has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the period of suspension expired?
      `I have lost or left the job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lost or voluntarily left the employment?
      `my hours with another employer since the suspension began` IS A NUMBER @desc Since the suspension began, how many hours of insurable employment have you accumulated with another employer?
      `the hours I need to qualify` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you need to qualify for benefits (section 7 or 7.1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not entitled to benefits because I am suspended for misconduct` IF
    `s 31 the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits`
        `I am suspended from my job because of my misconduct`
        `my period of suspension has expired`
        `I have lost or left the job`
        `my hours with another employer since the suspension began`
        `the hours I need to qualify`

@export Am I not entitled to receive benefits because I took a period of leave without just cause (s 32(1))?
GIVEN `I took a period of leave from my job without just cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily take a period of leave from your employment without just cause?
      `my employer authorized the leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer authorize the period of leave (before or after it began)?
      `we agreed on the day I would return` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you and your employer agree on the day on which you would resume employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not entitled to benefits because I took leave without just cause` IF
    `s 32(1) the claimant who takes leave is disentitled` `I took a period of leave from my job without just cause` `my employer authorized the leave` `we agreed on the day I would return`

@export Has my disentitlement for a period of leave ended (s 32(2))?
GIVEN `I have resumed the employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you resumed the employment?
      `I have lost or left the job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lost or voluntarily left the employment?
      `my hours with another employer since the leave began` IS A NUMBER @desc Since the leave began, how many hours of insurable employment have you accumulated with another employer?
      `the hours I need to qualify` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours of insurable employment do you need to qualify for benefits (section 7 or 7.1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my disentitlement for taking leave ended` IF
    `s 32(2) the disentitlement has ended` `I have resumed the employment` `I have lost or left the job` `my hours with another employer since the leave began` `the hours I need to qualify`

@export Am I not entitled to receive benefits because I lost or left a job within three weeks before its set term ended or my lay-off date (s 33(1))?
GIVEN `I lost the job because of my misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose the employment because of your misconduct?
      `I left the job without just cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you voluntarily leave the employment without just cause?
      `my only reason for being disentitled is that I left or refused a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your only possible reason for being disentitled that you left, or refused to accept, an employment?
      `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to join, or not join, a union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By remaining in or accepting the employment, would you have lost the right to become, or refrain from becoming, a member of an association, organization or union of workers?
      `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to stay in and follow the rules of my union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By remaining in or accepting the employment, would you have lost the right to continue to be a member of such a union and to observe its lawful rules?
      `the day I lost or left the job` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you lose or leave the employment (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)?
      `my job was for a set term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the employment for a set term?
      `the day the set term expires` IS A DATE @desc If it was for a set term, on what day does the term expire (ISO 8601)? If not, give any date.
      `my employer had already given me notice of a lay-off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your employer already given you notice that you would be laid off?
      `the day I was to be laid off` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day were you to be laid off (ISO 8601)? If not, give any date.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not entitled to benefits because I lost or left a job just before its end` IF
    `s 33(1) the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits`
        `I lost the job because of my misconduct`
        `I left the job without just cause`
        (`ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies`
            (`s 35 the claimant is not disqualified or disentitled under sections 30 to 33`
                `my only reason for being disentitled is that I left or refused a job`
                `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to join, or not join, a union`
                `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to stay in and follow the rules of my union`))
        `the day I lost or left the job`
        (IF `my job was for a set term` THEN JUST `the day the set term expires` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `my employer had already given me notice of a lay-off` THEN JUST `the day I was to be laid off` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Is my disentitlement for losing or leaving a job just before its end still in force on this day (s 33(2))?
GIVEN `I am not entitled under section 33(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you not entitled to benefits under section 33(1)?
      `the day in question` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking (ISO 8601)?
      `the day the term expired or I was to be laid off` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the set term expire, or were you to be laid off (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disentitlement for an anticipated loss still in force on this day` IF
    `s 33(2) the disentitlement is still in force on the day` `I am not entitled under section 33(1)` `the day in question` `the day the term expired or I was to be laid off`

@export Is my disentitlement under section 31, 32 or 33 suspended for a week in which I am otherwise entitled to special benefits (s 34)?
GIVEN `I am disentitled under section 31, 32 or 33` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you disentitled under section 31, 32 or 33?
      `I am otherwise entitled to benefits for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the disentitlement, are you otherwise entitled to benefits for the week?
      `the reason for those benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc For what reason would you otherwise get those benefits? One of: "a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)" (regular benefits), "pregnancy", "caring for a new-born or adopted child", "a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine", "care or support of a family member", "care or support of a critically ill child", "care or support of a critically ill adult". If you are not otherwise entitled to any benefits give any one.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my disentitlement suspended for this week` IF
    `s 34 the disentitlement is suspended for the week` `I am disentitled under section 31, 32 or 33` `I am otherwise entitled to benefits for the week` `the reason for those benefits`

@export Does the union exception protect me from being disqualified or disentitled only because I left or refused a job (s 35)?
GIVEN `my only reason for being disqualified or disentitled is that I left or refused a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your only possible reason for being disqualified or disentitled that you left, or refused to accept, an employment?
      `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to join, or not join, a union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By remaining in or accepting the employment, would you have lost the right to become, or refrain from becoming, a member of an association, organization or union of workers?
      `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to stay in and follow the rules of my union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By remaining in or accepting the employment, would you have lost the right to continue to be a member of such a union and to observe its lawful rules?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the union exception protect me` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies`
        (`s 35 the claimant is not disqualified or disentitled under sections 30 to 33`
            `my only reason for being disqualified or disentitled is that I left or refused a job`
            `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to join, or not join, a union`
            `staying in or taking the job would have cost me my right to stay in and follow the rules of my union`)

§§ `Labour disputes, prison and being outside Canada (ss 36 and 37)`
-- The first question only arises if the person lost or cannot resume a job because of a work stoppage; the second if the person is in
-- prison or outside Canada.

@export Am I not entitled to receive benefits because of a work stoppage caused by a labour dispute at my workplace (s 36)?
GIVEN `I lost my job or cannot resume it because of a work stoppage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you lose your employment, or are you unable to resume it, because of a work stoppage?
      `the dispute is between employers and employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute between employers and employees?
      `the dispute is between employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute between employees and employees?
      `it is connected with employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute connected with the employment of any persons?
      `it is connected with non-employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute connected with the non-employment of any persons?
      `it is connected with terms or conditions of employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute connected with the terms or conditions of employment of any persons?
      `the work stoppage is attributable to that dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work stoppage attributable to that labour dispute?
      `the stoppage is at the premises where I worked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the work stoppage at the factory, workshop or other premises at which you were employed? (Separate departments on the same premises, of branches commonly run as separate businesses, count as separate factories or workshops.)
      `the work stoppage has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the work stoppage ended (regulation 53: the work-force and the level of activity are each back to at least 85% of normal)?
      `I am now regularly engaged elsewhere in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become regularly engaged elsewhere in insurable employment?
      `I am otherwise entitled to benefits for the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Apart from the work stoppage, are you able to show that you are otherwise entitled to benefits for the period?
      `the reason for those benefits` IS A `Reason for benefits` @desc For what reason would you otherwise get those benefits? One of: "a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)" (regular benefits), "pregnancy", "caring for a new-born or adopted child", "a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine", "care or support of a family member", "care or support of a critically ill child", "care or support of a critically ill adult". If you are not otherwise entitled to any benefits give any one.
      `I am otherwise entitled to benefits under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you able to show that you are otherwise entitled to benefits by virtue of section 25 (a referred course, program or activity)?
      `I had expected to be absent for a reason entitling me to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the work stoppage, had you anticipated being absent from your employment for a reason entitling you to those benefits?
      `I had begun making arrangements for that absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the work stoppage, had you begun making arrangements in relation to that absence?
      `I can prove I am not taking part in the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you are not participating in the labour dispute?
      `I can prove I am not financing the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you are not financing the labour dispute?
      `I can prove I have no direct interest in the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you prove that you are not directly interested in the labour dispute?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not entitled to benefits because of a work stoppage` IF
    `s 36 the claimant is disentitled on the day`
        (`s 36(1) the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits`
            `I lost my job or cannot resume it because of a work stoppage`
            (`s 2(1) labour dispute` `the dispute is between employers and employees` `the dispute is between employees` `it is connected with employment` `it is connected with non-employment` `it is connected with terms or conditions of employment`
                AND `the work stoppage is attributable to that dispute`
                AND `the stoppage is at the premises where I worked`)
            `the work stoppage has ended`
            `I am now regularly engaged elsewhere in insurable employment`)
        (`s 36(3) the disentitlement is suspended for the period` `I am otherwise entitled to benefits for the period` `the reason for those benefits` `I am otherwise entitled to benefits under section 25` `I had expected to be absent for a reason entitling me to them` `I had begun making arrangements for that absence`)
        (`s 36(4) this section does not apply to the claimant` `I can prove I am not taking part in the dispute` `I can prove I am not financing the dispute` `I can prove I have no direct interest in the dispute`)

@export Does section 36(5) treat my department as a separate factory or workshop for the labour dispute rule?
GIVEN `separate branches of work commonly run as separate businesses in separate premises are run in separate departments on the same premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are separate branches of work, commonly carried on as separate businesses in separate premises, carried on in separate departments on the same premises?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 36(5) treat my department as a separate factory or workshop` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 36(5) each department is a separate factory or workshop` `separate branches of work commonly run as separate businesses in separate premises are run in separate departments on the same premises`)

@export Am I not entitled to receive benefits for a period when I am in prison or outside Canada (s 37)?
GIVEN `I am an inmate of a prison or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an inmate of a prison or similar institution?
      `I am not in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you outside Canada?
      `the Regulations allow an exception for my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Regulations make an exception for your case (regulation 54: parole, day parole, temporary absence or a certificate of availability to seek work; regulation 55: for example medical treatment abroad, or up to seven days for a funeral or to visit a seriously ill family member)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not entitled to benefits because I am in prison or outside Canada` IF
    `s 37 the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits for the period` `I am an inmate of a prison or similar institution` `I am not in Canada` `the Regulations allow an exception for my case`

§§ `Penalties, rescission and warnings (ss 38 to 41.1)`
-- This group only arises if the Commission has found, or may find, that the person made a false or misleading statement or failed to
-- declare earnings, so the form can ask "Has the Commission raised a penalty against you?" before showing it.

@export Can the Commission impose a penalty on me, or on a person acting for me, for something done or left undone in my claim (s 38(1))?
GIVEN `the Commission has become aware of facts that in its opinion establish one of these acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission become aware of facts that in its opinion establish one of the acts or omissions below?
      `I made a representation in a claim that I knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In relation to a claim for benefits, did you (or the person acting for you) make a representation that you knew was false or misleading?
      `I gave information or made a representation I was required to give that I knew was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Being required by the Act or the regulations to provide information, did you provide information or make a representation that you knew was false or misleading?
      `I knowingly failed to declare some or all of my earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly fail to declare to the Commission all or some of your earnings for a period for which you claimed benefits?
      `I made a claim or declaration that I knew was false or misleading because I did not disclose facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a claim or declaration that you knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts?
      `I knowingly negotiated a special warrant for benefits I was not entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Being the payee of a special warrant, did you knowingly negotiate or attempt to negotiate it for benefits to which you were not entitled?
      `I knowingly failed to return a special warrant or an excess amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly fail to return a special warrant, the amount of the warrant, or an excess amount, as section 44 requires?
      `I imported or exported a Commission document to defraud or deceive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you import or export a document issued by the Commission, or have it imported or exported, to defraud or deceive the Commission?
      `I took part in, agreed to or went along with one of those acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you participate in, assent to or acquiesce in any of those acts or omissions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission impose a penalty on me` IF
    `s 38(1) the Commission may impose a penalty on the claimant or a person acting for the claimant`
        `the Commission has become aware of facts that in its opinion establish one of these acts`
        `I made a representation in a claim that I knew was false or misleading`
        `I gave information or made a representation I was required to give that I knew was false or misleading`
        `I knowingly failed to declare some or all of my earnings`
        `I made a claim or declaration that I knew was false or misleading because I did not disclose facts`
        `I knowingly negotiated a special warrant for benefits I was not entitled to`
        `I knowingly failed to return a special warrant or an excess amount`
        `I imported or exported a Commission document to defraud or deceive`
        `I took part in, agreed to or went along with one of those acts`

@export What is the most the Commission can set as the penalty for one act or omission of mine (s 38(2))?
GIVEN `a benefit period was established for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a benefit period established for you?
      `the penalty is for failing to declare earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the penalty for knowingly failing to declare earnings for a period for which you claimed benefits (section 38(1)(c))?
      `my rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your rate of weekly benefits, in dollars? (0 if no benefit period was established.)
      `the amount deducted from my benefits for undeclared earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount was deducted from your benefits under section 19(3), in dollars? (0 if none.)
      `the benefits I would have been paid without that deduction or disentitlement` IS A NUMBER @desc What benefits would have been paid to you for that period if the deduction had not been made and you had not been disentitled or disqualified, in dollars? (0 if none.)
      `the maximum rate of weekly benefits when I acted` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the maximum rate of weekly benefits in effect when the act or omission occurred, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the Commission can set as my penalty` IS
    `s 38(2) the most the Commission may set as the amount of the penalty`
        `a benefit period was established for me`
        `the penalty is for failing to declare earnings`
        `my rate of weekly benefits`
        `the amount deducted from my benefits for undeclared earnings`
        `the benefits I would have been paid without that deduction or disentitlement`
        `the maximum rate of weekly benefits when I acted`

@export Are weeks of regular benefits I repaid because of such an act treated as weeks paid for the purposes of section 145(2) (s 38(3))?
GIVEN `I repaid weeks of regular benefits because of an act or omission in section 38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you repaid weeks of regular benefits as a result of an act or omission mentioned in section 38(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the weeks I repaid treated as weeks paid` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 38(3) the repaid weeks are deemed to be weeks of regular benefits paid for the purposes of subsection 145(2)` `I repaid weeks of regular benefits because of an act or omission in section 38(1)`)

@export Is it too late for the Commission to impose a penalty on me (s 40)?
GIVEN `a prosecution for the act has been started against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a prosecution for the act or omission been started against you?
      `the day of my act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the act or omission occur (ISO 8601, e.g. 2020-01-15)?
      `the day the penalty would be imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the penalty be imposed (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it too late for the Commission to impose a penalty on me` IF
    `s 40 a penalty shall not be imposed` `a prosecution for the act has been started against me` `the day of my act or omission` `the day the penalty would be imposed`

@export Can the Commission rescind or reduce a penalty it imposed on me (s 41)?
GIVEN `new facts have been presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have new facts been presented to the Commission?
      `the Commission is satisfied the penalty was imposed by mistake or without knowing a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission rescind or reduce my penalty` IF
    `s 41 the Commission may rescind the imposition of the penalty, or reduce it` `new facts have been presented` `the Commission is satisfied the penalty was imposed by mistake or without knowing a material fact`

@export Can the Commission give me a warning instead of setting a penalty (s 41.1(1))?
GIVEN `the Commission could set a penalty for my act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could the Commission set the amount of a penalty for your act or omission under section 38(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission give me a warning instead of a penalty` IF
    `s 41.1(1) the Commission may issue a warning instead of setting the amount of a penalty` `the Commission could set a penalty for my act or omission`

@export Can a warning still be issued to me on this day (s 41.1(2))?
GIVEN `the day of my act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the act or omission occur (ISO 8601, e.g. 2020-01-15)?
      `the day the warning would be issued` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the warning be issued (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a warning still be issued to me on this day` IF
    `s 41.1(2) a warning may be issued on the day` `the day of my act or omission` `the day the warning would be issued`

§§ `Assigning benefits, repayment and debts to the Crown (ss 42 to 47)`
-- This group only arises if the person owes, or may owe, money to the Crown or a government, or has been paid benefits they may have
-- to repay.

@export Is a transaction that purports to assign my benefits, or to give them as security, void (s 42(1))?
GIVEN `the transaction concerns my benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the transaction concern your benefits?
      `it appears to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give them as security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give the benefits as security?
      `it is a recovery or deduction under section 42(2) or 42(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a recovery of an amount, or a deduction, that section 42(2) or 42(3) allows?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a transaction assigning my benefits void` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies`
        (`s 42(1) a transaction appearing to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give benefits as security is void`
            `the transaction concerns my benefits`
            `it appears to assign, charge, attach, anticipate or give them as security`
            `it is a recovery or deduction under section 42(2) or 42(3)`)

@export Can the Commission recover an amount I owe under the Act out of my benefits (s 42(2))?
GIVEN `I owe the amount under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount payable by you under the Act?
      `it must be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the amount be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account?
      `benefits are payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are benefits payable to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission recover an amount I owe out of my benefits` IF
    `s 42(2) the amount may be recovered out of the benefits payable to the person` `I owe the amount under the Act` `it must be credited to the Employment Insurance Operating Account` `benefits are payable to me`

@export How much may the Commission deduct from my benefits to pay a government for an advance or welfare payment it made me (s 42(3))?
GIVEN `a government paid me an advance or assistance or a welfare payment for a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Government of Canada, a provincial or municipal government, or another prescribed authority, pay you an advance, assistance or a welfare payment for a week?
      `it would not have been paid if benefits had been paid for that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the payment not have been paid if unemployment benefits had been paid for that week?
      `benefits later became payable to me for that week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did unemployment benefits later become payable to you for that week?
      `I consented beforehand to the deduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On or before receiving the payment, did you consent to the Commission deducting it from your benefits and paying it to the government?
      `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was the advance, assistance or welfare payment, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may the Commission deduct from my benefits for a government payment` IS
    -- 0 when the conditions are not met: the Commission may deduct nothing.
    CONSIDER `s 42(3) the amount the Commission may deduct and pay`
                 (`s 42(3) the Commission may deduct from the benefits and pay to the government or authority`
                     `a government paid me an advance or assistance or a welfare payment for a week`
                     `it would not have been paid if benefits had been paid for that week`
                     `benefits later became payable to me for that week`
                     `I consented beforehand to the deduction`)
                 `the amount of the payment`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN 0
    WHEN JUST a   THEN a

@export Am I liable to repay an amount the Commission paid me as benefits (s 43)?
GIVEN `it was paid for a period for which I am disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amount paid to you as benefits for a period for which you are disqualified?
      `I was not entitled to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amount paid to you as benefits to which you were not entitled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to repay an amount paid to me as benefits` IF
    `s 43 the claimant is liable to repay the amount` `it was paid for a period for which I am disqualified` `I was not entitled to it`

@export How much am I liable to repay of the benefits the Commission paid me (s 43)?
GIVEN `it was paid for a period for which I am disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amount paid to you as benefits for a period for which you are disqualified?
      `I was not entitled to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the amount paid to you as benefits to which you were not entitled?
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the Commission pay you as benefits for that period, or without entitlement, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much am I liable to repay of the benefits paid to me` IS
    `s 43 the amount the claimant is liable to repay`
        (`s 43 the claimant is liable to repay the amount` `it was paid for a period for which I am disqualified` `I was not entitled to it`)
        `the amount paid`

@export How much must I return to the Commission without delay (s 44)?
GIVEN `a payment to which I was disentitled` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did you receive or obtain as a benefit payment to which you are disentitled, in dollars? (0 if none.)
      `the excess over what I was entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc By how much does a benefit payment you received or obtained exceed the amount to which you are entitled, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I return without delay` IS
    `s 44 the amount the person shall return without delay` `a payment to which I was disentitled` `the excess over what I was entitled to`

@export How much must I pay the Receiver General because earnings for a period I was paid benefits were later paid to me (s 45)?
GIVEN `I received benefits for a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive benefits for a period?
      `someone became liable to pay me earnings for the same period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Under an arbitration award, court judgment or otherwise, did an employer, trustee in bankruptcy or other person later become liable to pay you earnings (including damages for wrongful dismissal) for the same period?
      `they paid me those earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that person pay you the earnings?
      `the benefits that would not have been paid had the earnings been paid in time` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the benefits that would not have been paid if the earnings had been paid, or payable, when the benefits were paid, in dollars (worked out under the Regulations' rules on earnings)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I pay the Receiver General when earnings for a benefit period are later paid` IS
    `s 45 the amount the claimant shall pay to the Receiver General` `I received benefits for a period` `someone became liable to pay me earnings for the same period` `they paid me those earnings` `the benefits that would not have been paid had the earnings been paid in time`

@export How much will my employer or another payer deduct from earnings owed to me and remit to the Receiver General (s 46(1))?
GIVEN `someone has become liable to pay me earnings for a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an employer, trustee in bankruptcy or other person become liable to pay you earnings (including damages for wrongful dismissal) for a period?
      `they have reason to believe benefits were paid to me for that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that person have reason to believe that benefits have been paid to you for that period?
      `the amount that would be repayable under section 45` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount would be repayable under section 45 if the earnings were paid to you, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will be deducted from earnings owed to me` IS
    `s 46(1) the amount to deduct from the earnings payable to the claimant and remit to the Receiver General` `someone has become liable to pay me earnings for a period` `they have reason to believe benefits were paid to me for that period` `the amount that would be repayable under section 45`

@export Does the 36-month limit mean no amount is payable under section 45 or deductible from my earnings under section 46(1) (s 46.01)?
GIVEN `the day of my lay-off or separation` IS A DATE @desc On what day were you laid off or separated from the employment in relation to which the earnings are paid or payable (ISO 8601, e.g. 2020-01-15)?
      `the day the repayment would be determined` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the repayment be determined (ISO 8601)?
      `the Commission thinks the cost of determining it would equal or exceed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Commission's opinion, would the administrative costs of determining the repayment likely equal or exceed the amount of the repayment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the 36-month limit mean nothing is payable or deductible` IF
    `s 46.01 no amount is payable under section 45 or deductible under subsection 46(1)` `the day of my lay-off or separation` `the day the repayment would be determined` `the Commission thinks the cost of determining it would equal or exceed it`

@export Is an amount I owe under sections 38, 39, 43, 45, 46 or 46.1 a debt due to the Crown (s 47(1))?
GIVEN `I owe it under one of those sections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount payable by you under section 38, 39, 43, 45, 46 or 46.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an amount I owe a debt due to the Crown` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 47(1) the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` `I owe it under one of those sections`)

@export Can the Commission deduct and keep what I owe out of benefits that become payable to me (s 47(2))?
GIVEN `I owe an amount that is a debt to the Crown under section 47(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you owe an amount that is a debt due to Her Majesty under section 47(1)?
      `benefits have become payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have benefits become payable to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission deduct what I owe out of my benefits` IF
    `s 47(2) the amount of the indebtedness may be deducted and retained out of the benefits` `I owe an amount that is a debt to the Crown under section 47(1)` `benefits have become payable to me`

@export Can the Commission still recover an amount I owe, or is it more than 72 months since the liability arose (s 47(3) and (4))?
GIVEN `the liability follows a reconsideration under section 52` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount one the Commission decided on reconsidering your claim under section 52 as benefits you were not qualified for or entitled to?
      `the day the Commission notified me of the amount` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day did the Commission notify you of the amount (ISO 8601)? If not, give any date.
      `the day my liability otherwise arose` IS A DATE @desc If not, on what day did the liability arise (ISO 8601)?
      `the days an appeal or review was pending` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days within the 72 months was an appeal or other review of a decision establishing the liability pending?
      `the day the Commission would try to recover it` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the Commission try to recover the amount (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission still recover what I owe` IF
    `s 47(3) the amount may still be recovered`
        (CONSIDER `s 52(3)(b) the day on which the liability arises for the purposes of subsection 47(3)` `the liability follows a reconsideration under section 52` `the day the Commission notified me of the amount`
         WHEN NOTHING  THEN `the day my liability otherwise arose`
         WHEN JUST d   THEN d)
        `the days an appeal or review was pending`
        `the day the Commission would try to recover it`

§§ `Making and proving my claim (ss 48 to 53)`

@export Are the conditions on which a benefit period may be established for me met (s 48(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `I made an initial claim in accordance with section 50 and the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an initial claim for benefits in accordance with section 50 and the regulations?
      `I proved I am qualified to receive benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you proved that you are qualified to receive benefits?
      `I supplied the information in the form and manner the Commission directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you supplied information in the form and manner directed by the Commission?
      `it gave my employment circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information give your employment circumstances?
      `it gave the circumstances of my interruption of earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the circumstances pertaining to any interruption of your earnings?
      `the Commission requires other information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission require other information from you?
      `I supplied that other information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you supplied that other information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the conditions for establishing a benefit period for me met` IF
        `s 48(1) the first condition on which a benefit period may be established is met` `I made an initial claim in accordance with section 50 and the regulations` `I proved I am qualified to receive benefits`
    AND `s 48(2) the second condition on which a benefit period may be established is met` `I supplied the information in the form and manner the Commission directed` `it gave my employment circumstances` `it gave the circumstances of my interruption of earnings` `the Commission requires other information` `I supplied that other information`

@export Has the Commission done what it must after receiving my initial claim (s 48(3))?
GIVEN `the Commission has received my initial claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission received your initial claim for benefits?
      `the Commission has decided whether I am qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided whether you are qualified to receive benefits?
      `the Commission has notified me of its decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission notified you of its decision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Commission done what it must after receiving my initial claim` IF
    `s 48(3) the Commission has done what it must on receiving the initial claim` `the Commission has received my initial claim` `the Commission has decided whether I am qualified` `the Commission has notified me of its decision`

@export Have I done what is needed to be entitled to receive benefits for this week (s 49(1))?
GIVEN `I made a claim for this week in accordance with section 50 and the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a claim for benefits for this week in accordance with section 50 and the regulations?
      `I proved I meet the requirements for receiving benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you proved that you meet the requirements for receiving benefits?
      `I proved that nothing disentitles or disqualifies me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you proved that no circumstances or conditions exist that have the effect of disentitling or disqualifying you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what is needed to be entitled to benefits for this week` IF
    `s 49(1) the person has done what is needed to be entitled to receive benefits for the week` `I made a claim for this week in accordance with section 50 and the regulations` `I proved I meet the requirements for receiving benefits` `I proved that nothing disentitles or disqualifies me`

@export Must the Commission give me the benefit of the doubt on whether I am disqualified or disentitled (s 49(2))?
GIVEN `the question is whether I am disqualified under section 30 or disentitled under section 31, 32 or 33` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question whether circumstances exist that disqualify you under section 30 or disentitle you under section 31, 32 or 33?
      `the evidence on each side is equally balanced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the evidence on each side of that question equally balanced?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission give me the benefit of the doubt` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 49(2) the claimant is given the benefit of the doubt on the issue` `the question is whether I am disqualified under section 30 or disentitled under section 31, 32 or 33` `the evidence on each side is equally balanced`)

@export Has the Commission done what it must after receiving my claim for this week (s 49(3))?
GIVEN `the Commission has received my claim for this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission received your claim for benefits for this week?
      `the Commission has decided whether benefits are payable for the week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided whether benefits are payable to you for that week?
      `the Commission has notified me of its decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission notified you of its decision?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Commission done what it must after receiving my claim for the week` IF
    `s 49(3) the Commission has done what it must on receiving the claim for the week` `the Commission has received my claim for this week` `the Commission has decided whether benefits are payable for the week` `the Commission has notified me of its decision`

@export Was my claim made as directed, at the office or place it must be made (s 50(2))?
GIVEN `I made it in the manner directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the claim in the manner directed?
      `I made it at the office that serves the area where I live` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it at the office of the Commission that serves the area in which you live?
      `I made it at another place the Commission prescribed or directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make it at another place that is prescribed or that the Commission directed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my claim made as directed at the proper place` IF
    `s 50(2) the claim is made as directed at the proper place` `I made it in the manner directed` `I made it at the office that serves the area where I live` `I made it at another place the Commission prescribed or directed`

@export Was my claim made on the proper form (s 50(3))?
GIVEN `I completed a form the Commission supplied or approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the claim by completing a form supplied or approved by the Commission?
      `I completed it as the Commission's instructions say` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you complete it in the manner set out in the Commission's instructions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was my claim made on the proper form` IF
    `s 50(3) the claim is made on the proper form` `I completed a form the Commission supplied or approved` `I completed it as the Commission's instructions say`

@export Did I make my claim for the week within the prescribed time (s 50(4))?
GIVEN `the day I made my claim for the week` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you make the claim for the week (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-20)?
      `the last day I could make a claim for that week` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day on which you could make a claim for that week in time? (Regulation 26: normally within three weeks after the week claimed; within one week after it if you made no claim for four or more consecutive weeks.) ISO 8601.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I make my claim for the week within the prescribed time` IF
    `s 50(4) the claim for the week is made within the prescribed time` `the day I made my claim for the week` `the last day I could make a claim for that week`

@export Have I met the Commission's requirement to give additional information about my claim (s 50(5))?
GIVEN `the Commission required additional information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission required you to provide additional information about your claim?
      `I provided it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the requirement to give additional information` IF
    `s 50(5) the requirement to provide additional information is met` `the Commission required additional information` `I provided it`

@export Have I met the Commission's requirement to make my claim or give information in person (s 50(6))?
GIVEN `the Commission required me to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission required you (or your group or class of claimants) to be at a suitable place at a suitable time to make a claim or give information in person?
      `I was there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you there at that time?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the requirement to attend in person` IF
    `s 50(6) the requirement to attend in person is met` `the Commission required me to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` `I was there`

@export Have I met the Commission's requirement to register for employment (s 50(7))?
GIVEN `the Commission required me to register for employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission required you to register for employment at an agency administered by the Government of Canada or a provincial government?
      `I registered and reported when told` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you registered and reported to the agency at the reasonable times it or the Commission directed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the requirement to register for employment` IF
    `s 50(7) the requirement to register for employment is met` `the Commission required me to register for employment` `I registered and reported when told`

@export Have I met the Commission's requirement to prove I am making reasonable and customary efforts to find suitable work (s 50(8))?
GIVEN `the Commission required me to prove my efforts to find work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission required you to prove that you are making reasonable and customary efforts to obtain suitable employment?
      `I proved my efforts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you proved it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the requirement to prove my efforts to find work` IF
    `s 50(8) the requirement to prove efforts to obtain employment is met` `the Commission required me to prove my efforts to find work` `I proved my efforts`

@export Have I met the Commission's requirement to give an additional medical certificate (s 50(8.1))?
GIVEN `the Commission required an additional certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission required you to provide an additional certificate from a medical doctor or nurse practitioner, to prove the conditions for compassionate care or family caregiver benefits?
      `I provided it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the requirement to give an additional certificate` IF
    `s 50(8.1) the requirement to provide an additional certificate is met` `the Commission required an additional certificate` `I provided it`

@export Have I met the requirement to give the mailing address of my normal place of residence (s 50(9))?
GIVEN `I gave the mailing address of my normal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided the mailing address of your normal place of residence?
      `the Commission permitted me not to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission otherwise permitted you not to?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met the requirement to give my mailing address` IF
    `s 50(9) the requirement to provide a mailing address is met` `I gave the mailing address of my normal place of residence` `the Commission permitted me not to`

@export May the Commission waive or vary a condition or requirement of section 50 for my benefit (s 50(10))?
GIVEN `the Commission is of the opinion that my circumstances warrant a waiver or variation for my benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Commission's opinion, do the circumstances warrant a waiver or variation of the condition or requirement for the benefit of you, or of your class or group of claimants?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission waive or vary a condition or requirement for my benefit` IF
    `s 50(10) the Commission may waive or vary a condition or requirement` `the Commission is of the opinion that my circumstances warrant a waiver or variation for my benefit`

@export Am I not entitled to receive benefits because a condition or requirement under section 50 is not met (s 50(1))?
GIVEN `my claim was made as directed at the proper place, or that was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim made as directed at the proper place (s 50(2)), or was that waived?
      `my claim was made on the proper form, or that was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim made on the proper form (s 50(3)), or was that waived?
      `my claim for the week was in time, or that was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim for the week made within the prescribed time (s 50(4)), or was that waived?
      `I gave the additional information required, or it was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given any additional information the Commission required (s 50(5)), or was that waived?
      `I attended in person as required, or it was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you attended in person as the Commission required (s 50(6)), or was that waived?
      `I registered for employment as required, or it was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you registered for employment as the Commission required (s 50(7)), or was that waived?
      `I proved my efforts as required, or it was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you proved your efforts to find work as the Commission required (s 50(8)), or was that waived?
      `I gave the additional certificate as required, or it was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the additional certificate the Commission required (s 50(8.1)), or was that waived?
      `I gave my mailing address, or it was waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given the mailing address of your normal place of residence (s 50(9)), or was that waived?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I not entitled to benefits because a condition or requirement under section 50 is not met` IF
    `s 50(1) the claimant is not entitled to receive benefits for as long as a condition or requirement is not met`
        `my claim was made as directed at the proper place, or that was waived`
        `my claim was made on the proper form, or that was waived`
        `my claim for the week was in time, or that was waived`
        `I gave the additional information required, or it was waived`
        `I attended in person as required, or it was waived`
        `I registered for employment as required, or it was waived`
        `I proved my efforts as required, or it was waived`
        `I gave the additional certificate as required, or it was waived`
        `I gave my mailing address, or it was waived`

@export Must the Commission give me and my employer a chance to give information about why I lost or left my job (s 51(a))?
GIVEN `the documents on my claim indicate I lost my job through misconduct or left it voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission find an indication, from the documents relating to your claim, that the loss of employment resulted from your misconduct or that you voluntarily left employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission give me and my employer a chance to give information` IF
    `s 51(a) the claimant and the employer are to be given an opportunity to provide information about the reasons for the loss of employment` `the documents on my claim indicate I lost my job through misconduct or left it voluntarily`

@export Must the Commission take the information I gave about why I lost or left my job into account (s 51(b))?
GIVEN `the documents on my claim indicate I lost my job through misconduct or left it voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission find an indication, from the documents relating to your claim, that the loss of employment resulted from your misconduct or that you voluntarily left employment?
      `I gave the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided the information about the reasons for the loss of employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission take my information into account` IF
    `s 51(b) the Commission must take the information into account in determining the claim` `the documents on my claim indicate I lost my job through misconduct or left it voluntarily` `I gave the information`

@export Can the Commission still reconsider my claim for benefits (s 52(1) and (5))?
GIVEN `the day the benefits were paid or would have been payable` IS A DATE @desc On what day were the benefits paid, or would they have been payable (ISO 8601, e.g. 2024-01-15)?
      `the Commission thinks a false or misleading statement was made in connection with my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Commission's opinion, was a false or misleading statement or representation made in connection with your claim?
      `the day the Commission would reconsider` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the Commission reconsider the claim (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission still reconsider my claim` IF
    `s 52(1) and (5) the Commission may reconsider the claim on the day` `the day the benefits were paid or would have been payable` `the Commission thinks a false or misleading statement was made in connection with my claim` `the day the Commission would reconsider`

@export Must the Commission calculate the money and tell me its decision after reconsidering my claim (s 52(2))?
GIVEN `the Commission decided I received money I was not qualified or entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided that you received money by way of benefits for which you were not qualified or to which you were not entitled?
      `the Commission decided I did not receive money I was qualified and entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided that you did not receive money for which you were qualified and to which you were entitled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commission calculate the money and tell me its decision` IF
    `s 52(2) the Commission must calculate the amount of the money and notify the claimant of its decision` `the Commission decided I received money I was not qualified or entitled to` `the Commission decided I did not receive money I was qualified and entitled to`

@export Is the amount the Commission calculated on reconsidering my claim repayable under section 43 (s 52(3))?
GIVEN `the Commission decided I received money I was not qualified or entitled to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided that you received money by way of benefits for which you were not qualified or to which you were not entitled?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the amount calculated on reconsideration repayable under section 43` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 52(3)(a) the amount calculated is repayable under section 43` `the Commission decided I received money I was not qualified or entitled to`)

@export How much money is payable to me because the Commission decided I was qualified and entitled but was not paid (s 52(4))?
GIVEN `the Commission decided I was qualified and entitled to money by way of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission decided that you were qualified and entitled to receive money by way of benefits?
      `the money was not paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the money not paid to you?
      `the amount the Commission calculated` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount did the Commission calculate, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is payable to me because I was not paid` IS
    -- 0 when the conditions are not met: nothing is payable under s 52(4).
    CONSIDER `s 52(4) the amount payable to the claimant` `the Commission decided I was qualified and entitled to money by way of benefits` `the money was not paid to me` `the amount the Commission calculated`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN 0
    WHEN JUST a   THEN a

@export May the Commission notify me of its decision in this way (s 53)?
GIVEN `the Commission must notify me of a decision under Part I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission required to notify you of a decision under Part I of the Act?
      `the Commission considers this way of notifying me adequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider the manner of notifying you adequate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Commission notify me in this way` IF
    `s 53 the person may be notified in that manner` `the Commission must notify me of a decision under Part I` `the Commission considers this way of notifying me adequate`

@export Can the Commission count my hours of insurable employment by a method other than the one the Regulations set (s 55(2))?
GIVEN `the Commission considers it is not possible to apply the regulations to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consider that it is not possible to apply the provisions of the regulations on how many hours of insurable employment you have?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission count my hours by another method` IF
    `s 55(2) the Commission may authorize an alternative method of establishing how many hours of insurable employment a person has` `the Commission considers it is not possible to apply the regulations to me`

@export Can the Commission make an agreement with me, as an employee, on another way of counting hours of insurable employment (s 55(4))?
GIVEN `I am an employer or an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an employer or an employee (the Commission may make such agreements with either)?
      `the agreement would provide for another way of counting hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the agreement provide for an alternative method of establishing how many hours of insurable employment persons have?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission agree another way of counting hours with me` IF
    `s 55(4) the Commission may enter into the agreement` `I am an employer or an employee` `the agreement would provide for another way of counting hours`

§§ `Employment support measures and the National Employment Service (Part II)`
-- This group only arises if the person asks for, or receives, help under an employment support measure, or is referred by the national
-- employment service, so the form can ask "Do you ask for help under an employment support measure?" before showing it.

@export Have I made the commitments the guidelines expect of a person receiving assistance under an employment support measure (s 57(1)(e))?
GIVEN `I am committed to achieving the goals of the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you committed to achieving the goals of the assistance?
      `I am committed to taking primary responsibility for identifying my employment needs and locating services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you committed to taking primary responsibility for identifying your employment needs and locating the services necessary to allow you to meet them?
      `sharing the cost of the assistance is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it appropriate for you to share the cost of the assistance?
      `I am committed to sharing the cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you committed to sharing the cost of the assistance?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I made the commitments expected of a person receiving assistance` IF
    `s 57(1)(e) the commitment expected of persons receiving assistance is made` `I am committed to achieving the goals of the assistance` `I am committed to taking primary responsibility for identifying my employment needs and locating services` `sharing the cost of the assistance is appropriate` `I am committed to sharing the cost`

@export Has the Commission worked in concert with the provinces and consulted workers and employers as the Act requires (s 57(2))?
GIVEN `the Commission works in concert with provincial governments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission work in concert with provincial governments on employment support measures?
      `the Commission consults workers and employers to align measures with labour market needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission consult with workers and employers to align employment support measures with labour market needs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Commission worked in concert and consulted as the Act requires` IF
    `s 57(2) the Commission has worked in concert and consulted as the Act requires` `the Commission works in concert with provincial governments` `the Commission consults workers and employers to align measures with labour market needs`

@export Am I an insured participant, who can ask for help under an employment support measure (s 58)?
GIVEN `I am employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed in insurable employment?
      `I have been employed in insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been employed in insurable employment (an insured person is one who is or has been)?
      `I am asking for assistance under an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you requesting assistance under an employment support measure?
      `a benefit period is established for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When you ask for the assistance, is a benefit period established for you?
      `I have had a benefit period that ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you had a benefit period that has ended?
      `the day my benefit period ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day did it end (ISO 8601, e.g. 2021-06-01)? If not, give any date.
      `the number of the last 10 years I paid premiums with no refund` IS A NUMBER @desc In how many of the last 10 years did you pay employee's premiums that did not entitle you to a refund under subsection 96(4)?
      `I received the emergency response benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been in receipt of the employment insurance emergency response benefit?
      `the last day I received the emergency response benefit` IS A DATE @desc If so, what was the last day you received it (ISO 8601)? If not, give any date.
      `the day I ask for the assistance` IS A DATE @desc On what day do you ask for the assistance (ISO 8601, e.g. 2026-06-01)?
      `regulation 76.11 includes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you within regulation 76.11 (a person who has a benefit period under a provincial plan, or had one end within the previous 60 months, and who would have been entitled to special benefits under section 22 or 23 had they not been entitled to provincial benefits)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an insured participant` IF
    `s 58 the person is an insured participant`
        `I am employed in insurable employment`
        `I have been employed in insurable employment`
        `I am asking for assistance under an employment support measure`
        `a benefit period is established for me`
        (IF `I have had a benefit period that ended` THEN JUST `the day my benefit period ended` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the number of the last 10 years I paid premiums with no refund`
        (IF `I received the emergency response benefit` THEN JUST `the last day I received the emergency response benefit` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the day I ask for the assistance`
        `regulation 76.11 includes me`

@export Can the Commission establish an employment support measure to help me obtain or keep employment (s 59)?
GIVEN `the measure is to help insured participants and other workers get or keep work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the measure meant to help insured participants and other workers, including workers in groups underrepresented in the labour market, to obtain or keep employment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission establish a measure to help me obtain or keep employment` IF
    `s 59 the Commission may establish the employment support measure` `the measure is to help insured participants and other workers get or keep work`

@export Has the Commission maintained a national employment service that gives information on jobs across Canada (s 60(1))?
GIVEN `the Commission maintains a national employment service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission maintain a national employment service?
      `it gives information on employment opportunities across Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it provide information on employment opportunities across Canada to help workers find suitable employment and employers find suitable workers?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Commission maintained the national employment service` IF
    `s 60(1) the Commission has maintained the national employment service as the Act requires` `the Commission maintains a national employment service` `it gives information on employment opportunities across Canada`

@export Has the Commission collected employment information and made it available to me as the Act requires (s 60(2)(a))?
GIVEN `the Commission collects information on employment for workers and workers seeking employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission collect information concerning employment for workers and workers seeking employment?
      `it makes the information available as it considers necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it make the information available to the extent it considers necessary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the Commission collected and made available employment information` IF
    `s 60(2)(a) the Commission has collected and made available the information as the Act requires` `the Commission collects information on employment for workers and workers seeking employment` `it makes the information available as it considers necessary`

@export Is the referral the national employment service made to me, or refused me, within what the Act allows (s 60(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the referral discriminates on a prohibited ground` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the referral (or the refusal to refer you) discriminate on a prohibited ground of discrimination within the meaning of the Canadian Human Rights Act?
      `the referral discriminates because of political affiliation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it discriminate because of political affiliation?
      `it gives effect to a bona fide occupational requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give effect to a limitation, specification or preference based on a bona fide occupational requirement?
      `it gives effect to a special program, plan or arrangement under section 16 of the Canadian Human Rights Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give effect to a special program, plan or arrangement mentioned in section 16 of the Canadian Human Rights Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the referral made to me within what the Act allows` IF
    `s 60(2)(b) the referral is as the Act requires` `the referral discriminates on a prohibited ground` `the referral discriminates because of political affiliation` `it gives effect to a bona fide occupational requirement` `it gives effect to a special program, plan or arrangement under section 16 of the Canadian Human Rights Act`

@export Is the Commission's decision about an employment support measure closed to review under section 112 (s 64)?
GIVEN `the decision is about an employment support measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the decision a decision of the Commission made in relation to employment support measures?
      `it is a decision to impose a penalty under section 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a decision under section 65.1 (a penalty for a person given financial assistance)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the decision about an employment support measure closed to review` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 64 the decision is not subject to review under section 112` `the decision is about an employment support measure` `it is a decision to impose a penalty under section 65.1`)

@export How much am I liable to repay of the financial assistance paid to me under section 61 (s 65)?
GIVEN `the principal and interest on a loan to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much principal and interest is owed on a loan made to you under section 61, in dollars? (0 if none.)
      `the amount paid on a guarantee or suretyship of my loan` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was paid on a guarantee or suretyship of a loan made to you, in dollars? (0 if none.)
      `the amount paid to me that I was not entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How much was paid to you that you were not entitled to, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much am I liable to repay of the financial assistance` IS
    `s 65 the amount the person is liable to repay` `the principal and interest on a loan to me` `the amount paid on a guarantee or suretyship of my loan` `the amount paid to me that I was not entitled to`

@export Can the Commission impose a penalty on me because of what I did about the financial assistance paid to me (s 65.1(1))?
GIVEN `financial assistance was provided to me under section 61` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was financial assistance provided to you under section 61?
      `the Commission has become aware of facts that in its opinion establish one of these acts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission become aware of facts that in its opinion establish one of the acts or omissions below?
      `I made a false or misleading representation in my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In relation to your application or request for the assistance, did you make a representation that you knew was false or misleading?
      `I made a false or misleading declaration by not disclosing facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In relation to your application or request, did you make a declaration that you knew was false or misleading because of the non-disclosure of facts?
      `I failed to attend or complete the course or activity, or was expelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Without good cause, did you fail to attend, carry out or complete the course, program or activity for which the assistance was provided, or were you expelled from it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission impose a penalty on me about my financial assistance` IF
    `s 65.1(1) the Commission may impose a penalty on the person` `financial assistance was provided to me under section 61` `the Commission has become aware of facts that in its opinion establish one of these acts` `I made a false or misleading representation in my application` `I made a false or misleading declaration by not disclosing facts` `I failed to attend or complete the course or activity, or was expelled`

@export What is the most the Commission can set as a penalty on me for one act or omission about my financial assistance (s 65.1(2))?
GIVEN `the amount of financial assistance provided to me` IS A NUMBER @desc How much financial assistance was provided to you, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the Commission can set as my penalty about financial assistance` IS
    `s 65.1(2) the most the Commission may set as the amount of the penalty` `the amount of financial assistance provided to me`

@export Is it too late for the Commission to impose a penalty on me about my financial assistance (s 65.1(3))?
GIVEN `a prosecution for my act or omission has been started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a prosecution for the act or omission been started against you?
      `the day of my act or omission` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the act or omission occur (ISO 8601, e.g. 2020-01-15)?
      `the day the penalty would be imposed` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the penalty be imposed (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it too late to impose a penalty on me about my financial assistance` IF
    `s 65.1(3) the penalty shall not be imposed` `a prosecution for my act or omission has been started` `the day of my act or omission` `the day the penalty would be imposed`

@export Can the Commission rescind or reduce a penalty it imposed on me about my financial assistance (s 65.1(4))?
GIVEN `new facts have been presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have new facts been presented to the Commission?
      `the Commission is satisfied the penalty was imposed by mistake or without knowing a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission satisfied that the penalty was imposed without knowledge of, or on the basis of a mistake as to, some material fact?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission rescind or reduce my penalty about financial assistance` IF
    `s 65.1(4) the Commission may rescind the imposition of the penalty, or reduce it` `new facts have been presented` `the Commission is satisfied the penalty was imposed by mistake or without knowing a material fact`

@export Is an amount I must repay under section 65, or a penalty under section 65.1, a debt due to the Crown (s 65.2(1))?
GIVEN `it is repayable under section 65 or is a penalty under section 65.1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the amount repayable by you under section 65, or a penalty imposed on you under section 65.1?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I must repay or pay as a penalty a debt due to the Crown` IF
    `ei2 seat: a JUST TRUE answer means the provision applies` (`s 65.2(1) the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` `it is repayable under section 65 or is a penalty under section 65.1`)

@export Can the Commission recover what I owe out of an amount that becomes payable to me under section 61 (s 65.2(2))?
GIVEN `I owe an amount of indebtedness under section 65.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you owe an amount that is a debt due to Her Majesty under section 65.2(1)?
      `an amount has become payable to me under section 61` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an amount become payable to you under section 61?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission recover what I owe out of an amount payable to me` IF
    `s 65.2(2) the indebtedness may be recovered out of the amount payable` `I owe an amount of indebtedness under section 65.2(1)` `an amount has become payable to me under section 61`

@export Can the Commission still recover what I owe under Part II, or is it more than 72 months since the liability arose (s 65.2(3))?
GIVEN `the day my liability arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the liability arise (ISO 8601, e.g. 2020-03-01)?
      `the day the Commission would try to recover it` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the Commission try to recover the amount (ISO 8601)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Commission still recover what I owe under Part II` IF
    `s 65.2(3) the amount may still be recovered` `the day my liability arose` `the day the Commission would try to recover it`
